<urn:atm:triage:finding/ARCH-AO26-F007>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ARCH-AO26-F007" ;
  triage:title "AST guard sweep silently drops non-Rust consumer file after ARCH-AO26-F002 fix" ;
  triage:description "PR #982 commit b484ebb48c2d2881b399273ab756be83e70ae3ab fixed ARCH-AO26-F002 by broadening the sqlite_writer_batch_window_is_private_to_storage guard's consumer sweep from 3 hardcoded files to ai11_guarded_workspace_sources() (all Rust files under crates/, excluding the test file). This is a regression relative to the original 3-file list, which included scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py -- a Python file outside crates/ that collect_rust_files does not walk, so it is now silently dropped from the sweep entirely. quality-mgr independently confirmed the Python file currently contains zero references to BATCH_TIME_BUDGET (no live leak today), so this is non-blocking, but the guard's own regression-prevention purpose no longer covers this benchmark-harness path. Recommended fix: re-add an explicit non-Rust check for scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py (and any other benchmark/smoke scripts outside crates/) alongside the new crate-wide Rust sweep, rather than relying solely on collect_rust_files." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ao2" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "architecture-boundary" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
